SELECT id, 'kg_400', '{"kg":"kg_400"}'::jsonb, 'KG 100–800 (1. Ebene)', '400 Building - Technical installations', 122, '{"designation":"Building - Technical installations","notes":"Construction services and supplies for the construction of technical installations of buildings, civil engineering structures and infrastructure facilities\nThis also includes the overarching measures in connection with the technical systems.\nThe individual technical installations include the associated frames, fastenings, fittings, heat and cold insulation, sound and fire protection measures, covers, panelling, paintwork, labelling and the measuring, control and regulation systems integrated at the factory. This also includes the operating costs up to acceptance.\nThe costs for creating and closing slots and ducts as well as pipe and cable trenches are generally recognised in KG 300.\nIn the case of conversions and modernisations, technical installations also include the costs of partial demolition, repair, securing and dismantling work. The costs must be recognised in the relevant cost groups.","level":1,"parent_kg":null,"kg1":"KG 400","kg2":null}'::jsonb, '\hline 400 & Building - Technical installations & \begin{tabular}{l}
Construction services and supplies for the construction of technical installations of buildings, civil engineering structures and infrastructure facilities \\
This also includes the overarching measures in connection with the technical systems. \\
The individual technical installations include the associated frames, fastenings, fittings, heat and cold insulation, sound and fire protection measures, covers, panelling, paintwork, labelling and the measuring, control and regulation systems integrated at the factory. This also includes the operating costs up to acceptance. \\
The costs for creating and closing slots and ducts as well as pipe and cable trenches are generally recognised in KG 300. \\
In the case of conversions and modernisations, technical installations also include the costs of partial demolition, repair, securing and dismantling work. The costs must be recognised in the relevant cost groups.
\end{tabular} \\' FROM regulation_tables WHERE standard_code = 'DIN-276' AND edition = '2018-12' AND table_code = 'TABLE1'
